---
import PengoLayout from "../layouts/PengoLayout.astro";
---

<PengoLayout
  title="About Pengo Systems"
  description="Pengo Systems builds products for the seams where work becomes action and consequences matter."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/about/"
  active="about"
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero section-shell">
      <h1>About Pengo Systems</h1>
      <p>
        Pengo Systems builds products for the seams where work becomes action and consequences matter.
      </p>
    </section>

    <article class="article-shell">
      <p>
        As AI and automation move deeper into real workflows, existing software plumbing is being asked to carry a new kind of load. Specs can become build instructions. Code changes can become deployments. Tool calls can cross systems. Payment, access, infrastructure, and workflow actions can become real.
      </p>

      <p>
        Many systems were built around human-paced review, manual judgment, and informal handoffs. Machine-to-machine work changes that rhythm. It can chain steps quickly, route around friction, and turn small gaps into real outcomes.
      </p>

      <p class="pull-line">
        The answer is not to rebuild everything.
      </p>

      <p>
        The answer is to add better checkpoints, observations, controls, and receipts at the points where consequence begins.
      </p>

      <p>
        Pengo products help teams see what is present, what is missing, what changed, what crossed a boundary, what action was attempted, and what proof exists afterward.
      </p>

      <p>
        We use AI where it helps — to extract, compare, draft, classify, and surface useful shape — but AI is not the authority. Pengo products are built around declared requirements, deterministic checks, bounded execution, and receipt-backed evidence.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our product family includes tools for artifact checks, repo/change mapping, AI output observation, callable boundary control, action gating, and evidence packeting.
      </p>

      <p>
        Pengo does not ask teams to replace the systems they already use. We build defensive layers that can be added around existing tools, workflows, and action surfaces so teams can implement controls faster, reduce blind spots, and produce evidence when it matters.
      </p>

      <p>
        Pengo helps teams control machine-to-machine work without pretending identity, prompts, logs, or dashboards are enough.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</PengoLayout>
